{
  "rules": [
    "Systematic Underestimation of Bullish Spikes: The model consistently fails to capture the magnitude of rapid price increases (e.g., the jump from ~76 to ~88 in late November), forecasting only linear, low-momentum growth. Correction: Apply a non-linear upward adjustment factor when the 3-day price momentum exceeds 3%.",
    "Sentiment Lag: Positive sentiment spikes (e.g., 0.50 on 2022-11-29) are not immediately reflected in the forecast trajectory, which remains flat or slowly rising. Correction: Immediately shift the forecast baseline upward by 2-3 EUR upon detecting a sentiment score > 0.4, rather than waiting for price confirmation.",
    "Failure to Anticipate Volatility Regime Shifts: The model assumes mean reversion to a narrow band (~76-80) even when the market enters a sustained high-volatility uptrend. Correction: Widen the forecast confidence interval and increase the slope coefficient during periods of sustained upward price acceleration.",
    "Overshoot Correction on Pullbacks: The model does not account for the sharp volatility and subsequent pullbacks seen after the peak (e.g., dropping from 89 to 77). Correction: Introduce a mean-reversion dampener in the forecast 10-15 days after a peak, reducing the projected price by 5-8% to align with historical volatility patterns.",
    "Horizon-Specific Bias: Errors are minimal for the first 1-2 days but grow exponentially thereafter. Correction: Apply a decaying correction factor that reduces the forecast slope by 15% for every day beyond the 5-day horizon."
  ]
}
